WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.880
Movie trailers in general are often guilty
of lying to us, and it seems that goes double

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:06.900
for Star Wars.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.040
The Rise of Skywalker trailers have made us
believe we're going to see a number of things

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.660
that probably won't happen, here's a look
at some of the biggest misdirects.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:20.440
One of the most surprising shots in the Rise
of Skywalker marketing comes from the second

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:24.280
trailer, which was released at the D23 Expo
in August.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:29.900
We're talking about the shot of Rey in a hooded
cloak, holding a lightsaber with two red beams.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.600
We've never seen a lightsaber like that in
a Star Wars movie, so it's an intriguing reveal

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:40.390
on its own, but then it unfolds into a double-ended
weapon reminiscent of Darth Maul's.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:45.579
Clearly, this shot is meant to make you wonder
if Rey will follow up on her Dark Side temptations

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.760
and go evil for the end of the trilogy.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.380
But no one really thinks that's going to happen,
right?

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:55.320
Especially after the marketing team for The
Last Jedi did…kind of the exact same thing

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.320
already.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:58.740
"I don't believe that."

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.660
A couple explanations come to mind.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:07.120
The first is that Rey is having a dream or
vision, like Luke did during his visit to

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.140
Dagobah in The Empire Strikes Back.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:13.900
Another possibility is that the dark version
of Rey is some kind of evil clone.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:18.880
We don't know for sure, but it seems the least
likely option is that this shining beacon

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.120
of hope will turn evil and stay that way in
the final installment of her trilogy.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.080
"It's not true."

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.820
Also seen in the second Rise of Skywalker
trailer is a brief but curious shot of everyone's

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:37.220
trusty and perpetually anxious protocol droid,
C-3PO, with conspicuously red eyes.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:42.760
The big implication here is that somehow C-3PO
has been tampered with in some way.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:47.880
The droid's red eyes are a first in his Skywalker
saga arc and they seem to imply that some

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.120
entity has infiltrated C-3PO.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.720
Why else would they go red?

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.880
"I'm so confused."

00:01:55.420 --> 00:02:00.900
C-3PO's red eyes seem like a misdirect, intended
to mislead viewers by encouraging them to

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.260
think that the droid has turned to the dark
side.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.160
Is it a temporary malfunction?

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:07.780
Maybe a simple problem with some faulty wiring?

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:12.060
Our favorite golden droid isn't getting any
younger, so it's not surprising that he might

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.640
need a tune-up or upgrade 40 years on.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.500
But the red eyes somehow indicating C-3PO
is going to become a tool for the dark side

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.560
is probably one idea we should definitely
drop.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:28.180
The final trailer for The Rise of Skywalker
features a shot of Rey and Kylo Ren fighting

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.700
side by side.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:34.700
Considering that plenty of other footage shows
them fighting each other, it's tough to gauge

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.400
what The Rise of Skywalker wants us to believe
about these characters.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.099
We've already seen Rey and Kylo Ren work together
to defeat Snoke and his guards in The Last

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:43.780
Jedi.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.920
They've also shared a connection through their
Force sensitivities, even communicating and

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.940
tracking one another's movements.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:54.480
It would be easy to think the Skywalker saga
was gearing up to make some grandiose statement

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:59.319
about finding and embracing the gray area
between the light and dark sides of the Force

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.920
and teaming up with your presumed enemy against
a far bigger threat.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:07.750
On the other hand, Rey and Kylo Ren returned
to their respective "teams" after defeating

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:11.520
Snoke in The Last Jedi and remained enemies
through the end of the film.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:16.260
By showing us scenes of them fighting against
and alongside each other, it's clear they

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.220
don't want us to know what actually happens.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:23.779
The big question that comes from the shot
of Rey and Kylo Ren teaming up in the trailer

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:26.100
is why they're doing it in the first place.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.880
Is there a mutual recognition of their power
and capabilities?

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:33.320
Are they really teaming up, or just trying
to exploit each other?

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:36.900
To keep all that a mystery, the marketing
is trying to have it both ways.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:42.339
Rey's backstory has been a mystery for Star
Wars fans ever since Episode Seven first came

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:43.440
out, years ago.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:47.379
She's essentially the main character of Star
Wars right now, and we really don't know a

00:03:47.379 --> 00:03:52.269
lot about her, past or present, other than
the fact that she's really, really good at

00:03:52.269 --> 00:03:53.319
using the Force.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:58.040
Very few clues have been dropped about her
life before we meet her in The Force Awakens.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:03.420
To date, all we know is that she was abandoned
on the planet Jakku, which led her to a life

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.960
of scavenging, believing she was nobody.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:10.839
Through interrogations and tense conversations,
Kylo Ren has frequently hinted that he knows

00:04:10.839 --> 00:04:16.130
the truth about Rey's past, including her
parents, who were apparently no one special,

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:19.340
"filthy junk traders" who sold her for drinking
money.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:21.740
"You have no place in this story.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:23.040
You come from nothing.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:23.820
You're nothing."

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:29.540
Knowing this makes one particular moment in
the Rise of Skywalker trailers all the more

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.240
intriguing.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:35.240
During the final trailer, as they face off
in the rain on a piece of wreckage, Rey is

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:39.800
seen looking at Kylo Ren while her voiceover
states, "Nobody knows me."

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.540
The camera cuts, revealing Kylo Ren as he
activates his lightsaber and his voiceover

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.480
replies, "But I do."

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:50.820
Putting these two shots and their corresponding
voiceover one after the other in the final

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:57.170
trailer certainly implies Kylo Ren will reveal
Rey's past, or some other potentially earth-shattering

00:04:57.170 --> 00:05:01.200
truth about her, that will change her direction
in The Rise of Skywalker.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.960
It's the kind of tease that gives you deja
vu.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.800
Haven't we already dealt with this issue?

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:09.420
Was Kylo lying before, or are the trailers
lying now?

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:12.960
Furthermore, does anyone even care who Rey's
family is at this point?

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:18.020
It wasn't Luke, it wasn't Leia, and it wasn't
Han, and it's probably not Lando.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.860
This late in the game, would a big reveal
about her parentage even matter?

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.160
It's probably Palpatine, isn't it.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.340
Maybe that's how we get evil Rey.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.240
Why not?

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.320
"This is where the fun begins."

